+##### limit
+
+The maximum number of ranges to take from one header, unset (no limit) by
+default. When the header has more valid ranges than `limit`, they are collapsed
+into a single range from the lowest start to the highest end, so that the
+response can be a single range rather than multipart. Ranges are counted after
+`combine` is applied.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(1000, 'bytes=500-600,0-10,20-30', { limit: 2 })
+// => [{ start: 0, end: 600 }]
+```
+
